Description: /**
 * @brief Output clustered 2D data and centroids as an EPS (Encapsulated PostScript) file.
 *
 * Generates EPS graphics for a set of 2D observations and their cluster centroids,
 * assigning each cluster a distinct color. The function scales and centers the plot
 * to fit a fixed-size canvas, and marks centroids with a special symbol.
 *
 * @param pts      Array of observations to plot. Must not be NULL and must have at least one element.
 * @param len      Number of observations in pts. Must be greater than 0.
 * @param cent     Array of cluster centroids. Must not be NULL and must have k elements.
 * @param k        Number of clusters. Must be positive.
 *
 * @return None.
 *
 * @note Output is written to stdout. The function allocates temporary memory internally and frees it before returning.
 */
Dependencies: None

